A Windows desktop tool that lets you select text from anywhere on your screen as if it were normal selectable text, even in images, scanned PDFs, videos or remote desktops. Press a hotkey, drag over the text, and it's copied to your clipboard and saved to a searchable session document. It can also clean up the text, translate it and guess where it came from using AI.

Final Year Project, BSc Business Information Systems, University College Cork (2026). Shortlisted for the university Final Year Project Award, one of 30 projects from over 140 students.

## How it works

1. Turn capture on with the power button on the Home tab.
2. Press **Ctrl+Q** in any app. The screen freezes and the text is scanned in the background.
3. Drag over the text. Words highlight live as you select.
4. Release to copy the text to the clipboard and save it to the current session. Press **Esc** to cancel.

## Features

**Capture**
- System-wide hotkey that works over any application
- Frozen-screen overlay with live word highlighting
- Two selection modes: **Native** (flows across lines like normal text selection and stays within one column) and **Box** (selects everything inside a rectangle)
- Floating mini toolbar in the overlay for switching translation, selection and format on the fly

**Two OCR engines**
- **Online:** Google Cloud Vision for high accuracy
- **Offline:** Tesseract with OpenCV preprocessing (denoising, contrast enhancement, sharpening, dark-background detection) for use without a connection or API key

**AI features (Gemini API, online mode)**
- **Deep Clean:** fixes broken line wraps, spacing and paragraph structure without changing meaning, with an automatic local fallback if the API is unavailable
- **Translation:** translate captures to English, keeping the original alongside if you want
- **Source guess:** identifies where a capture came from (page title, site and URL) by reading the browser address bar and the screenshot. It runs in the background so copying stays instant.

**Organising your captures**
- Sessions: group captures into named sessions
- Editable session document with manual saving
- Find in document with live highlighting and next/previous navigation
- Light and dark themes
- Local storage in a TinyDB JSON file

## Tech stack

| Area | Tools |
|------|-------|
| Language | Python |
| Main interface | PySide6 (Qt) |
| Capture overlay | Tkinter (separate event loop) |
| Online OCR | Google Cloud Vision API |
| AI | Gemini API |
| Offline OCR | Tesseract (pytesseract), OpenCV, NumPy |
| Storage | TinyDB |
| System integration | pynput (global hotkey), pyperclip (clipboard), Pillow (screen capture) |

## Design decisions

- **Moved from Tesseract to Google Cloud Vision.** My first prototype used Tesseract only. It was too slow on a full-screen capture, which broke the feel of selecting text. Cloud Vision cut the delay, and I kept Tesseract as an offline fallback.
- **Rebuilt line and word order from raw OCR.** Cloud Vision returns word boxes without line numbers, so I group words into lines by vertical position. That makes selection behave like real text instead of a rough rectangle.
- **Threaded by design.** OCR, translation and source guessing all run on worker threads, and a Qt signal bridge keeps UI updates thread-safe, so the overlay never freezes.

## Getting started

### Prerequisites

- Windows 10 or 11
- Python 3.10 or later
- A Google Cloud Vision API key (online mode)
- A Gemini API key (Deep Clean, translation, source guess)
- [Tesseract OCR](https://github.com/UB-Mannheim/tesseract/wiki) (offline mode)

### Installation

```bash
git clone https://github.com/senan22r/[REPO-NAME].git
cd [REPO-NAME]
pip install PySide6 pillow tinydb pyperclip pynput pytesseract opencv-python numpy
```

### API keys

Set environment variables:

```
VISION_API_KEY=your_vision_key
GEMINI_API_KEY=your_gemini_key
```

Or save each key in a text file next to the script (`vision_key.txt`, `gemini_key.txt`). Never commit these files.

### Run

```bash
python [main-file].py
```

## Project structure

```
[main-file].py   Main app: interface, overlay, selection, OCR, AI features
offline.py       Offline Tesseract OCR provider
```
